# Pico: project rules for Cursor

## What Pico is
A marketplace for short jobs. A worker proves one skill (verified score + level), a client posts a task with a minimum level and a reward, Pico assigns the closest verified worker, and the reward is held until the client releases it.
The former payment flow used Solana devnet with USDC. It is disabled in the marketplace UI while the product transitions to fiat; provider selection and integration are pending. Keep payment logic behind the domain layer and never hard-wire a provider into UI.

## Stack (current versions)
- Web app: `hackathon-krk/web`, Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Tailwind CSS 4.
- Data: Postgres on Supabase via `pg` 8.16, from Next.js route handlers only (`src/app/api/**`).
- Legacy chain code: Solana devnet, `@solana/web3.js` 1.98, `@solana/spl-token` 0.4, `@coral-xyz/anchor` 0.29. The app does not load a wallet provider.
- On-chain program: Anchor/Rust in `hackathon-krk/programs/pico` (built and deployed via Solana Playground). IDL copy lives in `web/src/idl/pico.json`.
- AI: `@google/genai` (Gemini) in `web/src/lib/gemini.ts`.
- Hosting: Vercel (project root is `hackathon-krk/web`).

## Code style
- TypeScript only. No `any`; use `unknown` and narrow. Explicit return types on exported functions.
- Functional React components and hooks. No class components.
- Server secrets (`OPERATOR_SECRET_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `POSTGRES_*`) are read only in server code. Never import them into client components, never log them.
- Never return raw DB errors to the client; strip connection strings (see `safeErr`).
- Small modules; one responsibility per file. Prefer editing an existing module over adding a parallel one.

## Architecture (layers, see `docs/architecture.md`)
- `src/platform/`: product rules (flow, roles, protections, capabilities). No I/O.
- `src/domain/`: how actions execute (API calls, Solana txs, storage). Must assert platform protections.
- `src/ui/` and `src/components/app/*View`: presentation only; read capabilities, call domain actions.
- `src/components/app/*Page.tsx`: controllers wiring hooks + capabilities + actions.
- `src/lib/`: infra (IDL, PDAs, constants, Solana helpers).
- UI never talks to the DB or chain directly.

## Domain terms
- Client (role `hire`): posts and pays for tasks. Worker (role `work`): claims and delivers.
- Account = marketplace account; payment identity/provider is not integrated yet.
- Task statuses: `draft`, `finding`, `assigned`, `progress`, `review`, `verification`, `revision`, `dispute`, `completed`, `cancelled`. Late statuses never move back to early ones.
- Claim: a worker takes a `finding` task; a second wallet gets HTTP 409 `taken`.
- Lock: funds reserved for a task. Release: payout to the worker, with an on-chain proof (tx signature).
- Reviewer fee: 10% of reward, locked when the reward changes.
- Skill: verified domain with `level` (Mid/Senior) and `score` (pass mark 75).

## Working rules
- Before changing API shapes, update `docs/api_contracts.md` in the same change.
- Before changing tables or integrations, update `docs/architecture.md`.
- Product scope and user flows live in `docs/product_requirements.md`; ask before building features not described there.

## Architecture & editing rules (Task.quo)

### Current product and entry points
- Task.quo (formerly Pico) is a short-task marketplace covering development,
  video and design. Paths below are relative to `hackathon-krk/web`.
- `/` (`src/app/page.tsx`) renders the public `LandingPage`; `/app/*` is the
  marketplace. Do not replace the landing or rename routes without a request.
- `src/app/app/layout.tsx` mounts `AppLanguageProvider` and `AppChrome`, not a
  wallet provider. `AccountSlot.tsx` isolates the header account slot; currently
  it displays payment availability, not working authentication.
- `src/components/app/PrototypePages.tsx` is a shared prototype-screen monolith;
  inspect all consumers before changing it. Home/tasks use prototype UI; task
  detail also retains a legacy fallback. `src/catalog/` is product skill data
  and must remain infrastructure-independent.

### Persistence and migration limitations
- `src/lib/db.ts` provides shared DB helpers/schema for `/api/pico/account` and
  `/api/pico/tasks` (`pico_accounts`, `pico_tasks`). `/api/waitlist` uses
  `pico_waitlist`. Schemas currently initialize at request time; use parameterized
  SQL and transactions for multi-step writes.
- `/api/pico` POST authentication still uses wallet signatures (`lib/auth.ts`).
  Non-wallet auth is unfinished: never bypass authentication to wire up UI.
  `/api/tools/run` is retired (HTTP 410).
- Solana removal is incomplete: `usePicoProgram()` returns null program/identity,
  `useConfig()` returns null, and task hooks use local demo data, not live chain
  reads. Payment-backed actions are disabled by UI/protections. A fiat provider
  is not selected/integrated. These guards are not a substitute for server auth.
- Remaining imports include `NewTaskPage`, `SlotTable`, `DemoControls`,
  `lib/constants`, `lib/pdas`, `lib/program`, demo/account helpers and domain
  actions. Do not add new Solana/Anchor code. New marketplace persistence and
  business logic must use API routes + Postgres through the existing layers.
  Do not remove remaining packages until their consumers are migrated, or enable
  paid actions before real auth, authorization and payments are verified.
- Earlier on-chain lock/release terms describe legacy behavior, not working fiat
  payments. Old Pico/AI-budget/hackathon briefs are historical references, not
  instructions to restore crypto integration.

### Localization, visual safety and honest copy
- Supply all new/changed user-facing strings (errors, notices and accessible
  labels included) in all five locales: `en`, `es`, `pl`, `de`, `uk`.
  Use `src/components/landingTranslations.ts`, `landingSectionsCopy.ts` and
  `src/components/app/AppLanguage.tsx` with the existing language provider.
  Hard-coded English in legacy screens is debt, not a pattern to copy.
- Scope new marketplace CSS under `.app.tq-app` in `src/app/globals.css`; reuse
  tokens and local component/BUTTONS guidance. Never change global fonts for a
  local fix. Keep form controls' `font-family: var(--font)` rule complete and
  separate from headings: no dangling comma/selectors. Check Hiring/Working
  controls and responsive layouts after shared CSS edits.
- Keep visual redesigns separate from business-rule changes. Do not invent
  stats, testimonials, guarantees or payment success. Label mock/demo records
  as illustrative, never as live customers, balances or completed work.

### Workflow and checks
- `develop` is development; `release` is production; `app-redesign` is the design
  branch. Never commit directly to `release` or silently change production settings.
- Inspect branch/status/diff first and preserve others' uncommitted work.
  Do not stage, commit, push, merge or deploy unless explicitly requested.
- From `hackathon-krk/web`: `yarn dev`; open `/app` for the platform, `/` for the
  landing. Typecheck with `yarn tsc --noEmit` (or `npx tsc --noEmit` with installed
  dependencies). Never run `yarn build` while the dev server runs; ask before
  stopping it. Markdown-only edits do not need a build/typecheck.
- Do not bypass protections, weaken auth, expose secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`,
  discard unrelated work, or claim checks/migration steps you have not verified.
